THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
======================================================

--- Video

FFmpeg 8.1.2 — ffmpeg.org
  Bundled as the JavaCPP Presets GPL build, Maven artifact
  org.bytedeco:ffmpeg:8.1.2-1.5.14:windows-x86_64-gpl (the macOS test builds
  use the -macosx-arm64-gpl / -macosx-x86_64-gpl classifiers of the same
  version). It is configured with --enable-gpl --enable-version3, so the
  build as a whole is under the GNU General Public License version 3 or
  later, the same licence as Naqi (full text in LICENSE). Decodes and
  encodes every video.

x264 (commit b35605ace3ddf7c1a5d67a2eb553f034aef41d55, X264_BUILD 165) —
  videolan.org/developers/x264.html
  GPL-2.0-or-later. Statically linked into that FFmpeg build (avcodec);
  encodes the filtered video. The build script fetches x264's "stable"
  branch; this is the commit that branch held when JavaCPP Presets 1.5.14
  was built (unchanged from 2025-06-08 through the 2026-08-10 release).

x265 3.4 — github.com/videolan/x265
  GPL-2.0-or-later. Statically linked into that FFmpeg build.

  The same build also links, under GPL-compatible terms, zlib, LAME, Speex,
  Opus, opencore-amr, vo-amrwbenc, OpenSSL, OpenH264, libvpx, FreeType,
  HarfBuzz, libxml2, SRT, libwebp, libaom, SVT-AV1, zimg, mfx_dispatch and
  nv-codec-headers. Their exact versions and download URLs are in the build
  script linked below.

JavaCPP 1.5.14 and JavaCPP Presets — github.com/bytedeco/javacpp-presets
  Apache License 2.0 (full text below), or GPL-2.0 with the Classpath
  Exception. The Java bindings to FFmpeg.

